ate today is 20th okay so  six days will be my 15th  year anniversary a 16-year  14 year anniversary from when i snow 15  years holy [ __ ] 20 21  yeah so be 15 years since my first  uh hellfire missile shot um jesus  and uh and i remember it as clear as if  it  happened yesterday no  um and after like  you know you never really think that you  can do it until it happens and after it  happened  um i was devastated like i was in i was  in shock  like i felt like i just did something  that i had no right to do  you know i took another human being's  life in such a gross way like they had  no way to fight back they had no way to  to i didn't look them in the eye i  didn't know who they were i didn't see  their face we just  ended their life and i watched a guy  slowly drain  his life out  and afterwards i left like i laughed  when people were celebrating in my  squadron people were like high-fiving  themselves as if they're like yeah we're  winning the war on terror yeah high five  yeah congratulations but i felt nothing  but sickness  in me and i left  and uh as i was driving i drove off base  and i called my mother and i cried to  her and i  as as a young man like i cried and i was  like i can't believe i did this i can't  believe that i  i did it i felt so sick um and i called  her every  after every shot to to tell her this and  the advice that she gave me was you know  i know that it's a horrible thing  but your being there and feeling bad  about it is a good thing because it  means that you'll make sure that  the wrong people don't need to die the  wrong people aren't going to be killed  but as i look back on as i reflect on my  time in the military  i'm not sure if there was a right person

